docs/v1.1.0/SPEC-OBSERVABILITY.md:69:The semantic-convention source used for WP-1101 is the OpenTelemetry GenAI conventions repository, [client inference](https://github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions-genai/blob/main/docs/gen-ai/client-inference.md), checked 2026-10-31. That document is marked **Development** and its current required client span attributes are `gen_ai.operation.name` and `gen_ai.provider.name`; `gen_ai.request.model` is conditionally required when available. Record the revision or release tag used when the release implementation is frozen; do not describe the moving `main` document as a versioned stable release. The general OpenTelemetry semantic-conventions registry identifies itself as 1.44.0, and marks moved legacy GenAI fields as deprecated. In particular, do not emit `gen_ai.system` (use `gen_ai.provider.name`), `gen_ai.usage.prompt_tokens` (use `gen_ai.usage.input_tokens`), or `gen_ai.usage.completion_tokens` (use `gen_ai.usage.output_tokens`). The legacy `gen_ai.prompt`, `gen_ai.completion`, `gen_ai.input.messages`, and `gen_ai.output.messages` fields are also deprecated or moved; this design omits them both for migration compatibility and because their contents can contain sensitive prompt/output data. See the [GenAI registry migration entries](https://opentelemetry.io/docs/specs/semconv/registry/attributes/gen-ai/) and the [registry version](https://opentelemetry.io/docs/specs/semconv/).
